From 5a635403720072adcd4ab03973c51932807f01fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:35:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] overview: keep finger-scroll live during a held card drag
 (user feedback 2026-10-26)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

While an overview card drag is held, the touchpad finger-scroll stream pans
the strip again instead of being swallowed by the hold — the "touchboard
cannot move the workspace" half of the report.

- Overview::beginNavigation accepts NavigationSource::Scroll while the hold
  is a card drag; middle-press keeps refusing (it has its own pointer-scroll
  path in handleMotion).
- Navigation during a live card drag is pan-only: the filmstrip step is
  never committed under a held card (updateNavigation and endNavigation),
  the release settles the pan without moving focus, and every strip move
  refreshes the drop through Overview::refreshDragTarget().
- endDrag settles an in-flight scroll navigation before the drop resolves
  (external review S2-2): releasing mid-pan must not leave the navigation
  armed to step the filmstrip or steal keyboard focus afterwards.
- Wheel notches are inert during a card drag (external review S3-2): they
  commit workspace/focus moves the pan-only contract forbids.
- Checks: overview_card_axis_pan.sh asserts the drop under the pointer at
  the settled panned position in world space (S2-3), and the new
  overview_card_release_mid_axis.sh pins the mid-pan release (focus kept).

Validated: both checks GREEN with the wave-1 controls; falsified both ways
(reverting the beginNavigation guard turns the axis check red; removing the
endDrag settle turns the release check red). The drop-target refresh itself
is not separable at these geometries — a no-op refreshDragTarget mutation
keeps the checks green because pre-pan and post-settle targets coincide —
so the settle sequencing is what the release check pins. Format and lint
clean.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
